  "summary": "Sri Ramachandra Medical College was started on 11 September 1985 by the Sri Ramachandra Educational and Health Trust of N. P. V. Ramasamy Udayar — the first privately owned medical college in Tamil Nadu — and was declared a deemed university in September 1994. Now SRIHER, at Ramachandra Nagar, Porur, it has twelve faculties spanning medicine, dentistry, pharmacy, nursing, physiotherapy, allied health, engineering and management. It holds NAAC's A++ (CGPA 3.53) and UGC Category I status.",
